  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100085",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-37859",
      "knowledge_point_id": "a28c4320-e2dd-5195-81ac-b910c2328691",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating a Repeated Integral Defined Over a Type I Region",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx=$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}([\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]_{1/x}^{4x})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2x}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{11}{6}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{11}{3}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{2}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{7}{6}",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
        "version": "revealed-ma-answer-v1",
        "feedback_sha256": "43adca3946998b491112098a6a35c477576423876f98dd3935b8fbdb433cb947"
