  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100085",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-132289",
      "knowledge_point_id": "69f6b2a7-7a3a-5c2c-90db-5aa321784048",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Double Integral Defined Over a Type I Region",
      "problem": "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}x\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}x\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[x{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{x}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\,y\\,]}_{{x}^{3}}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-{x}^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})dx & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{5}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
