  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100214",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-122554",
      "knowledge_point_id": "67b7ea90-38e0-54b5-b76e-816beb0d48f9",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Domain of a Vector Field",
      "problem": "Determine which of the following shaded regions depicts the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-y}\\,j\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}},\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-y}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the radical is positive. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n3-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<3.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{1},$ which is the interior of a circle of radius $\\sqrt{3},$ as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100214/assets/f9c3a22a56839165bfd6c3b05f78ca25053553532063192836d0332d2b070436.png)\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx-y=0\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{1},$ which is the entire plane ${R}^{2}$ with the line $y=x$ removed:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100214/assets/a1ef93cc90bdd59b922723c2c2aa2bd670b43e416923892c9db53b36ac6b7e57.png)\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by ${D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2},$ shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100214/assets/f70cab5ec58e63e1751faa65b575a20da748b3e8ee90cffac8f1f3b029bbbd79.png)",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "value": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100214/assets/559ffda45a088810dcaa81628b8767bfedc64ca7f6b7ebd82aebdb2ed4a7ba00.png",
