  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-132402",
      "knowledge_point_id": "40bbc65e-5ee4-5ce6-aaf7-d0f9968c0c51",
      "knowledge_point": "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Given",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385/assets/bfa591e51f42e8e52b67e61c23b02ea69b03bdecc1c4b815370ce6b2b0b5f213.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the $x$-axis and the curves $x={y}^{2}-4$ and $x=4-{y}^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385/assets/85d3faac9a27353a8ea5151b3a32f1065aecb02fd07e0b20727c35de0a7fb216.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}-4\\le x\\le 4-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{4-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{4-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{4-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{4-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{4-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{4-{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}-4}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-4}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
        "version": "revealed-ma-answer-v1",
        "feedback_sha256": "c613aa097903cb53b01cb0825ec3d58ab115de7161adbc3c7ed07f2623501d9c"
      },
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
