  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-132512",
      "knowledge_point_id": "2ccbe70d-24f4-5e9c-8536-9ccab99f571b",
      "knowledge_point": "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Not Given",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385/assets/d90e750755a9520328e99583bfc80d9498ed34eb1695ba4ecd55b688d5b0216f.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed between the curves $x={y}^{2}$ and $x=2-{y}^{2},$ above the $x$-axis, as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dA=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. \n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =2-{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{y}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=0,$ the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100385/assets/eeadcddee3bc966372613ded9304c723768e9b81cd0299ad14084a94c9348463.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{2-{y}^{2}}^{{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{2-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y+1}}\\,dx]dy",
              "option": "4",
